Package: qxync
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Kami <mlzxgzy@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/mlzxgzy/qxync
Description: QNAP Qsync-compatible on-demand sync client (prebuilt)
 qxync is an unofficial, third-party client for QNAP Qsync built on FUSE.
 It mounts a QNAP NAS share and keeps files as on-demand placeholders:
 listing a directory does not download file contents, and reading a file
 fetches only the blocks that are actually read. Fully cached files can be
 dehydrated again to reclaim local disk space, and a background daemon
 keeps the mount alive across login session expiry.
 .
 This package ships prebuilt binaries (the qxync CLI, the qxyncd per-user
 daemon and the qxync-gui Tauri application) plus a desktop entry, hicolor
 icons and systemd user units. It is repackaged from the upstream release
 tarball without recompilation and without stripping, so the debug symbols
 needed for readable backtraces are kept in the binaries.
 .
 See /usr/share/doc/qxync/README.Debian for service setup (systemd --user,
 loginctl enable-linger, one daemon per NAS connection) and
 /usr/share/doc/qxync/DISCLAIMER.md for the trademark and interoperability
 boundary.
